[[:db/retract 17592186122084 :answer-field/choices 17592186122085] [:db/retract 17592186122084 :answer-field/choices 17592186122086] [:db/retract 17592186122084 :answer-field/choices 17592186122087] [:db/retract 17592186122084 :answer-field/choices 17592186122088] [:db/retract 17592186122084 :answer-field/choices 17592186122089] {:db/id 17592186124492 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-75d038ad-b39f-5c52-a2ee-ada0d3f5df01"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124494 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f9a03134-8525-58b4-a224-da8d571c355f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186416596 :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ and $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\}$ be bases of ${R}^{3}.$ \nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & =2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}, \\\\ {b}_{2} & =4{c}_{1}-2{c}_{3}, \\\\ {b}_{3} & =2{c}_{1}-3{c}_{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & a & 2 \\\\ b & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & c & -3\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186323799 :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ and $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ be bases of ${R}^{2}.$ If ${b}_{1}=5{c}_{2}-3{c}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}=2{c}_{1}-4{c}_{2},$ find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ from $B$ to $C.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186394291 :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-75d038ad-b39f-5c52-a2ee-ada0d3f5df01" :question/id #uuid "75d038ad-b39f-5c52-a2ee-ada0d3f5df01" :question/math-academy-id "q-113116" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors of $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-99aa8a6d-990b-5e61-8b84-2888eb56d9f3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-99aa8a6d-990b-5e61-8b84-2888eb56d9f3" :answer-field/id #uuid "99aa8a6d-990b-5e61-8b84-2888eb56d9f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-53b1d470-247b-548b-b13d-bc66e9449c39" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bdb98ddb-73a6-5232-b35f-26201c89674c" "answer-16bee97f-7038-5e53-805e-c034d4f9aa98" "answer-7251156a-c21f-5adb-9ff9-bd33a768f1d5" "answer-53b1d470-247b-548b-b13d-bc66e9449c39"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bdb98ddb-73a6-5232-b35f-26201c89674c" :answer/id #uuid "bdb98ddb-73a6-5232-b35f-26201c89674c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16bee97f-7038-5e53-805e-c034d4f9aa98" :answer/id #uuid "16bee97f-7038-5e53-805e-c034d4f9aa98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7251156a-c21f-5adb-9ff9-bd33a768f1d5" :answer/id #uuid "7251156a-c21f-5adb-9ff9-bd33a768f1d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53b1d470-247b-548b-b13d-bc66e9449c39" :answer/id #uuid "53b1d470-247b-548b-b13d-bc66e9449c39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124914 :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B$ to the basis $C$ is given by \n${P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 9\\end{aligned}].$\nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$  ." :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 9\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 9-(-5)\\cdot (-6)}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-3}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186122084 :answer-field/correct "answer-c3bfcb95-4180-5b13-9c4f-4eca7f2802a4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-91a0872a-5de1-5bcf-bf96-cd7b7f09e1c4" "answer-c3bfcb95-4180-5b13-9c4f-4eca7f2802a4" "answer-da5b45fe-6463-5cf0-bb39-9946f196f0dc" "answer-20f58787-8399-5ca4-a011-8a6df79512f1" "answer-ef95b44c-9f4a-5eb2-8a32-5755e8f3f15d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91a0872a-5de1-5bcf-bf96-cd7b7f09e1c4" :answer/id #uuid "91a0872a-5de1-5bcf-bf96-cd7b7f09e1c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3bfcb95-4180-5b13-9c4f-4eca7f2802a4" :answer/id #uuid "c3bfcb95-4180-5b13-9c4f-4eca7f2802a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da5b45fe-6463-5cf0-bb39-9946f196f0dc" :answer/id #uuid "da5b45fe-6463-5cf0-bb39-9946f196f0dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20f58787-8399-5ca4-a011-8a6df79512f1" :answer/id #uuid "20f58787-8399-5ca4-a011-8a6df79512f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef95b44c-9f4a-5eb2-8a32-5755e8f3f15d" :answer/id #uuid "ef95b44c-9f4a-5eb2-8a32-5755e8f3f15d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186377851 :question/problem "Let $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]\\}$  be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $S$ as $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ and $\\{{e}_{1},{e}_{2}\\}$, respectively. Recall that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $S$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2}$ relative to the basis $B.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & {e}_{1} & {e}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 11 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 11 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{S\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-f9a03134-8525-58b4-a224-da8d571c355f" :question/id #uuid "f9a03134-8525-58b4-a224-da8d571c355f" :question/math-academy-id "q-113519" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}$ and $C=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\}$ be bases of ${R}^{2}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ and $\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ relative to the basis $C.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -8 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0710a289-e926-5692-b8d2-c99ac59e739f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0710a289-e926-5692-b8d2-c99ac59e739f" :answer-field/id #uuid "0710a289-e926-5692-b8d2-c99ac59e739f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a2788a1d-e2ab-584c-86fe-21bbcb38e3ab" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a20fd614-e995-59f1-8191-fd45b0182f75" "answer-c8e82d70-a589-5d2a-9e35-2278a91f4109" "answer-a2788a1d-e2ab-584c-86fe-21bbcb38e3ab" "answer-753fb253-4ce3-57c6-9f54-6bb8fae24d9a" "answer-344c3b89-889a-5113-860d-9f442b0f7b5f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a20fd614-e995-59f1-8191-fd45b0182f75" :answer/id #uuid "a20fd614-e995-59f1-8191-fd45b0182f75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8e82d70-a589-5d2a-9e35-2278a91f4109" :answer/id #uuid "c8e82d70-a589-5d2a-9e35-2278a91f4109" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2788a1d-e2ab-584c-86fe-21bbcb38e3ab" :answer/id #uuid "a2788a1d-e2ab-584c-86fe-21bbcb38e3ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-753fb253-4ce3-57c6-9f54-6bb8fae24d9a" :answer/id #uuid "753fb253-4ce3-57c6-9f54-6bb8fae24d9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-344c3b89-889a-5113-860d-9f442b0f7b5f" :answer/id #uuid "344c3b89-889a-5113-860d-9f442b0f7b5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}]
